<%bte.doc super="downloadPage.bte"%>
<%bte.tpl name=pageTitle %>Ladder Downloads<%/bte.tpl%>
<%bte.tpl name=description %>Download A freeware ASCII arcade game similar to Donkey Kong.<%/bte.tpl%>
<%bte.tpl name=keywords %>ladder, ladder, download, download, jar, java, jre, j2se<%/bte.tpl%>
<%bte.tpl name=downloadLinkText %><b>Download</b><%/bte.tpl%>
<%bte.tpl name=pageContent %>
<p><big><b><a href="http://java.sun.com/j2se/1.4/download.html" target="_new">Download</a></b></big> and install the Java2 Runtime Environment version 1.4 (J2SE JRE) from java.sun.com if you do not already have it installed.</p>

<p><big><b><a href="ladder.jar">Download</a></b></big> the latest version of Ladder (Executable Jar - 103k) <small>(<a href="alternate.html">Alternate download sites</a>)</small></p>

<p>All you need to do is double click the jar file to start Ladder.</p>

<p>Some systems may not support executable jar files correctly.  If double clicking on the jar file does not work, try the following command lines:<br>
<b>java&nbsp;-jar&nbsp;ladder.jar</b><br>
<b>java&nbsp;-classpath&nbsp;ladder.jar&nbsp;com.Ostermiller.Ladder.Ladder</b></p>
<%/bte.tpl%>
<%/bte.doc%>
